    "name": "Exclusive Resorts - Inquiry Form API (submit-form / validate-email)",
    "description": "Direct API-level coverage of the two backend endpoints behind the public membership-inquiry form (https://public-site.stage.exclusiveresorts.com/inquire/), captured by watching DevTools Network during real, clearly-fake form submissions and then replaying/varying that request shape directly.\n\nCloudFront/WAF note: production returns a hard 403 ('Generated by cloudfront') to non-browser HTTP clients, Postman included -- confirmed directly (see BUG-REPORT.md). Every request below now sends a Chrome User-Agent plus Origin/Referer/Accept-Language matching a real /inquire/ page load, on the chance this is a simple header-based rule. If you still get the CloudFront 403 page with these headers in place, that confirms the block is fingerprint-based (TLS/JA3), which no HTTP client can spoof -- at that point, use playwright/tests/api-endpoints.spec.ts instead, which runs the same requests from inside a real browser page and is confirmed working.\n\nSafety notes (please read before running):\n- API-01, API-04 and API-08 create real records in the CRM (there is no sandbox/staging variant of this endpoint available). Run each once, not in a loop, per the assignment's 'do not flood the form' constraint.\n- API-02, API-03, API-06 do NOT create leads (the server 502s before that would happen).\n- API-05 (SQL injection) is included but was NOT executed against production while authoring this collection -- see its request description for why, and what I'd do instead in a real engagement.\n- API-07 deliberately probes /validate-email/ (read-only) instead of /submit-form/ so latency can be measured 10x without creating 10 leads.\n\nRun everything: `newman run postman/collection.json -e postman/environment.json`\nRun a single request: use `--folder` or filter by name in the Postman UI.",
